title: "Heimdall Camera-Replay Study: Supplementary Data and Analysis Code"
repository-code: https://github.com/mihaly27/ocr-segmentation
url: https://github.com/mihaly27/ocr-segmentation/tree/main/heimdall-replay-study
authors:
  - family-names: "Szabó"
    given-names: "Mihály"
  - family-names: "Kovari"
    given-names: "Attila"
  - family-names: "Kertész"
    given-names: "Gábor"
abstract: >-
  Derived evidence and analysis scripts for a one-camera through-glass
  license plate recognition replay study. The package reconstructs fixed
  OCR gates and fixed, directly switched, and step-bounded threshold
  trajectories over 319 observations and 121 tracking lifetimes, and
  checks outcomes against eight jointly transcribed human-reference cases.
  The original PaddleOCR log, recovered configuration and dictionary,
  current dataset lists and review tables, and checkpoint digests are included.
  Historical validation membership and checkpoint-to-export identity remain
  unverified.
  It does not contain the full proprietary recognition engine, model
  weights, original run archives, or complete source videos.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - license plate recognition
  - camera replay
  - bounded adaptation
  - reproducibility
